`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
**Incremental compilation review complete.** The key finding is that Sylveste already HAS the right pattern in `gen-skill-compact.sh` (SHA256 manifest + `check_freshness()`), but it's isolated to one use case. Generalizing this pattern to SessionStart hooks, flux-drive triage, and artifact generation could save **10,000-30,000 tokens/hour** on active sessions.

The P1 finding — idle /loop ticks paying full re-orientation cost — maps directly to the TypeScript watch mode pattern: file watchers only trigger recompilation when mtimes change. Sylveste lacks the equivalent "nothing changed" short-circuit.
